      description: "Acid victims are a tragic example of surrealism. A perverted form of torture that strips a person of their dreams, normalcy, and identity along with their natural features.Their beauty comes from within, a symbol of survival, proof of perseverance. Taking the worst pain of your life and turning it into something scarred yet beautiful is not easy, but it’s what most acid-attacked victims do. They prove time and again that somebody’s darkness cannot taint them, nor can their iniquity break them. Their story rattles our souls and makes us wonder how someone can go through something so terrible and yet smile and give hope. Acid burning the flesh off the victim’s face and metamorphosing it into a marred version of it, yet somehow turning out cognizable brings out the surreal quality of it. It’s rare and strange and yet doused in awe and art. It is surrealism at its best. It is probably one of my favourite pieces and I believe it would be an honour to have this piece as a part of my portfolio.",
